WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.270
All small towns have their horror stories,
tales of places plagued by terrifying apparitions,

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:13.389
unseen forces, and something waiting in the
shadows to terrorize unsuspecting innocents.

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:18.859
Sometimes it's a bridge at the edge of town
where a man in a bunny suit stalks, wielding

00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:23.029
an ax and looking for drivers who wander off
of the main road.

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:27.750
Sometimes it's a cabin in the woods rumored
to house an old, gnarled witch who steals

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.300
people away and throws them into a giant soup
pot.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:36.770
Maybe it's a cursed hotel where wicked spirits
roam the halls, and the guests check-in, but

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.450
never check out.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.820
Or maybe, like the little town where 16-year-old
Mark lived, it's a haunted house.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:49.590
Ever since he was a little boy, Mark had been
terrified of the house at the end of the lane.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:55.380
He walked past it on his way to school each
morning, and on his way back in the late afternoon.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:59.690
The sight of it made his palms sweat, his
heart beat just a little faster.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:05.400
It had once been a grand Victorian manor,
with turrets and a wraparound porch, painted

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.010
a brilliant white.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:12.830
But over the years, the paint had faded to
a dingy yellow, peeling away from the rotting

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:13.830
wood.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.150
There were holes in the roof where the rain
and snow dripped through between the shingles.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:22.860
The windows were caked with dust and grime,
obscuring anything that might be hiding inside.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.540
Not that there should have been anything there.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.729
The house had been abandoned for decades.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:33.350
Still, whenever he passed it, Mark could swear
he felt the presence of something in there.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:38.000
Pacing, watching, waiting for him to come
inside.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.189
The stories around town didn't help.

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:44.079
His parents told him to ignore them, said
that people just liked to talk when there

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:49.020
was nothing else to do, to make up things
to be afraid of because their lives were too

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.550
boring otherwise, but he couldn't avoid it.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:56.610
On a Boy Scouts trip when he was twelve, Mark
had tried to cover his ears when the other

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.649
boys gathered around the campfire with him
turned the topic to the old house, but they

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:04.530
teased and taunted him until he listened.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:09.840
They leaned in, faces lit ghoulishly from
below by the flickering orange flames, and

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.130
whispered about the ghost that had taken up
residence in the house.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:19.250
A wealthy old woman had lived there a long,
long time ago, they said.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.330
She was cruel, with a nasty temper.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:27.200
Everyone in town knew to avoid her, knowing
she would throw things at them from her window,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.099
shout at them, even sic her guard dogs on
them.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:34.520
But one group of boys in town couldn't resist
giving her a good scare.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.659
They dressed up in all black, red devil masks
covering their faces, and broke into her house

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.909
late one night.

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:44.870
When she awoke, they were standing at the
foot of her bed, holding pitchforks and telling

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.150
her they had come to drag her to hell.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.830
Her heart stopped from pure terror at the
sight.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:54.569
But her spirit lingered in the house, swearing
revenge against anyone who ever dared cross

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:56.330
her threshold again.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.900
Especially teenage boys.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.130
Mark didn't sleep a wink the whole camping
trip after hearing that.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:07.420
He swore then and there that, no matter what,
he would never go into that house.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.420
But everyone can be bought, and everyone has
a price.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.400
For Mark, the price was a car.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.550
He had been saving up as best as he could,
but it was tough to get a job with no way

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.730
to transport himself there, and mowing lawns
for his neighbors wasn't the most lucrative

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.730
gig.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.110
So, when he learned that his neighbor Oliver,
home on a break from college, was getting

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.680
rid of his old car, he begged to buy it.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.299
He doubted Oliver would go for it, knowing
what a jerk the guy could be, but to Mark's

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:36.180
surprise, Oliver gave him an offer.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.790
"I'll tell you what..."

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.170
Oliver's face broke into a sadistic smile.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.100
"I'll give you the car.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.280
If you can spend the whole night in the house
at the end of the street.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.280
Alone."

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.540
"Are you serious?!"

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.840
Mark scoffed.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.129
"Dead serious.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.900
Make it to sunrise without freaking out and
bailing, and the car's yours.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:53.900
Do we have a deal?"

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.209
Oliver stuck out his hand to shake.

00:03:56.209 --> 00:04:00.673
Every nerve in Mark's body was screaming at
him to say no, but if he didn't agree, he

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.790
wouldn't be able to afford a car until he
was in college.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.799
With a defeated sigh, he took Oliver's hand.

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:07.799
"Deal."

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:11.620
But as night fell and Mark prepared to meet
Oliver outside of the derelict old house,

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.230
he could feel pangs of regret deep in his
stomach.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.760
What was he thinking?

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.530
Was a car really worth living his worst nightmare?

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.660
What if Oliver didn't honor the deal?

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.720
Or worse...what if the stories were actually
true?

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.060
He swallowed the lump in his throat as he
shoved a sandwich into his backpack.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:32.820
He had food, water, a blanket, a flashlight,
and his phone.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.530
Everything he should need to survive the night.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.789
It would be fine!

00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:36.850
...He hoped.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.790
"Wasn't sure if you'd show!"

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.949
Oliver smirked as Mark walked up to meet him
on the rickety front porch.

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:43.509
"Well, I did.

00:04:43.509 --> 00:04:48.410
I'm here," Mark fidgeted nervously, staring
up at the house, its windows gazing down at

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:49.970
him like large, dark eyes.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.970
"So, here are the rules: You have to stay
here until sunrise.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.020
You leave before then, the deal's off.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.020
No car for you.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.010
And you have to stay alone.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:02.169
No calling for help from your little friends
or your mommy and daddy.

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:06.090
I'll be back to check on you in the morning
and make sure you really did it.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.090
Got it?"

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.090
"Got it."

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:09.090
Mark nodded.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.090
"Good luck, I'm rooting for you.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:11.090
Really."

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.510
Oliver turned to leave, then glanced over
his shoulder for one final dig.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:16.250
"Oh, and: Watch out for the ghost.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.330
I hear if she gets you, there won’t even
be bones left over.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:20.330
Night!"

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.350
And with that, he walked away.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:26.010
Mark stared down at the doorknob, preparing
himself to walk inside.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.419
He could still leave.

00:05:27.419 --> 00:05:30.090
He could turn and run all the way back home.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.670
But then Oliver would be right, and he would
be a coward.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.750
No, he was going to do it.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.860
He wasn't some scared little kid anymore.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.710
It was just a big, empty house.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.710
Nothing more.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:46.300
He slowly turned the doorknob, pushed, and
with a long, low creak, the door opened to

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.229
the darkness within.

00:05:48.229 --> 00:05:52.090
Against his better judgment, Mark instinctively
called out, "Hello?"

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:54.419
There was, thankfully, no response.

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:56.979
Just his voice echoing in the vast, empty
room.

00:05:56.979 --> 00:06:00.790
He let out a small sigh of relief, and pulled
the flashlight out of his backpack, switching

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:01.790
it on.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:06.419
He cast its beam around the front room of
the house, illuminating water damage, cobwebs

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:11.449
that he could only hope were no longer housing
any spiders, and a whole lot of plastic-wrapped

00:06:11.449 --> 00:06:12.449
furniture.

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:16.659
As he walked into the living room, he was
struck by just how ordinary it all seemed.

00:06:16.659 --> 00:06:21.550
It was creepy, of course, like any place made
for living that had been deprived of its purpose

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.660
for too long, but it wasn't nearly as bad
as his imagination had built it up to be.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:32.360
He had been picturing black candles, symbols
drawn on the floor in blood, a skeleton perched

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.039
on the couch, bats hanging from the ceiling.

00:06:35.039 --> 00:06:37.099
But there was none of that.

00:06:37.099 --> 00:06:39.930
No ghosts, no signs of danger.

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:42.800
This was just...mostly sort of sad.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.070
Once a home, now just a house, emptied out
and left to decay.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.980
He could get through the night just fine.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:53.410
As soon as he thought that, he felt something
scurry across his foot, and let out a scream.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.630
The flashlight revealed it to be a large rat,
running from his sudden intrusion and looking

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.229
for a place to hide.

00:06:59.229 --> 00:07:01.680
He clutched at his chest, catching his breath.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.949
It's just an animal.

00:07:02.949 --> 00:07:03.949
It's fine.

00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:06.850
It's not going to hurt you, he reminded himself.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.919
Now that some of the mystery was gone, he
was starting to wonder what the rest of the

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:11.289
house looked like.

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:15.710
What had once been breathless fear was replaced
with a certain morbid curiosity.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.860
If he had to be here all night, he might as
well explore.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.580
Hey, he thought to himself with a smile.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.060
Exposure therapy really works!

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.690
Scared of a haunted house?

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.920
Just go roaming around inside in the middle
of the night.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:27.960
You'll be cured!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:32.669
He sat his backpack down next to the stairs,
keeping a grip on his flashlight, and began

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:35.819
to investigate the rest of his greatest childhood
fear.

00:07:35.819 --> 00:07:39.620
He walked through the dining room, taking
in the ornate chandelier hanging from the

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:44.069
ceiling, the long, long table fit for hosting
at least a dozen guests.

00:07:44.069 --> 00:07:49.050
He wandered into the kitchen, the appliances
rusty from neglect, the oven, and stove where

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.660
someone once prepared their nightly dinners.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:56.420
All the pieces of a life, strewn about like
an unfinished jigsaw puzzle with no one to

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:58.139
pick up the pieces.

00:07:58.139 --> 00:08:01.330
Suddenly, Mark heard something coming from
the other room.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:05.599
It couldn't be...but it sounded like footsteps
on the stairs.

00:08:05.599 --> 00:08:10.970
Someone, or something, walking down, descending
the staircase toward him.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:15.650
He held his breath, heart pounding so hard
he could hear it in his ears.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:19.930
The footsteps stopped, and the house was silent
once again.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:26.669
Then, slowly, deliberately, he heard the same
footsteps heading back up, until they faded

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:29.680
away, too quiet to hear anymore.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.840
That wasn't his imagination.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.680
He was not alone in the house.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.640
Carefully, he tiptoed back the way he came,
careful not to make too much noise walking

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.880
across the creaking floorboards.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:44.050
When he reached the stairs, he saw no signs
of anyone else.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:47.520
In fact, there was nothing there at all.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.870
Wait..where was his backpack?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:52.880
He scanned the floor, certain he had just
overlooked it, misremembered where he sat

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:53.880
it down.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.900
But no matter where he looked, it wasn't there.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:01.269
His stomach dropped with a sudden realization:
whoever he had heard coming down the stairs

00:09:01.269 --> 00:09:02.649
must have taken it!

00:09:02.649 --> 00:09:06.790
He thought briefly about abandoning it, just
running out the front door and never looking

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.650
back, but...his phone was in there!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.580
If his parents found out, he'd be grounded
for months!

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.040
Not to mention, he wouldn't have a phone.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.450
But what if whoever took it was dangerous?

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:20.529
He couldn't be sure, but something in his
gut told him he needed to go upstairs and

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:21.529
check it out.

00:09:21.529 --> 00:09:24.310
He considered the weight of the flashlight
in his hand.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:27.990
If someone attacked him, would it be enough
to defend himself?

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:29.550
He sure hoped so.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:34.970
With shaky hands and unsteady legs, he began
to climb the stairs to the second floor of

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.089
the house.

00:09:36.089 --> 00:09:40.260
Maybe whoever had taken his backpack was just
as scared of him as he was of them?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.709
It was a comforting thought, though the comfort
was short-lived.

00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:50.030
As he started down the upstairs hall, preparing
to search the first bedroom, he heard a door

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.360
creak open behind him.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.910
He turned, and froze in wide-eyed terror at
the sight.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:01.870
There was a figure there emerging from the
shadows, a pale woman with long, dark hair,

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:06.100
wearing a white nightgown, reaching out to
him with a clawed hand.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:07.250
"Get...out..."

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.620
A voice rasped.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:12.630
Mark shrieked, dropped the flashlight, and
tore back down the stairs.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:17.260
He ran to the front door, but as his hand
touched the doorknob, a hand grabbed his ankle

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.260
and pulled.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.230
He toppled over, landing on the ground with
a painful thud.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.459
"Please..." He sobbed, shaking from fear.

00:10:23.459 --> 00:10:24.459
"Don't hurt me.

00:10:24.459 --> 00:10:25.459
I'll leave.

00:10:25.459 --> 00:10:26.459
I'll leave.

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:27.459
I'm so sorry.

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:28.459
Don't kill me!"

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:32.640
He braced himself for an unearthly voice,
for pain, but instead he heard gleeful cackling.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.600
He opened his eyes and saw Oliver standing
above him.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.870
"I knew you couldn't do it.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.260
You're such a chicken."

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:40.260
He smirked.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.260
"W-what?"

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.260
Mark stammered.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.550
"Come on, did you really think I was gonna
give you my car?

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:44.779
Are you stupid?"

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:46.279
Oliver scoffed.

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:47.279
"Clearly."

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:50.019
Mark followed the sound of the new voice,
coming from the stairs.

00:10:50.019 --> 00:10:53.630
There was Chase, one of Oliver's equally awful
friends.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.610
"He still believes in haunted houses.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:56.709
Did you like my work?

00:10:56.709 --> 00:10:58.000
Made it myself."

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:02.920
He held up what Mark could now see was a prop,
a mannequin dressed up like some kind of ghostly

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:03.920
woman.

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.430
"You gave it a good try, but I think it's
time for you to run along home now," Oliver

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.430
sneered.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.910
"Yeah, run home- oof!"

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.389
Chase's taunt was cut off, as he fell against
the banister suddenly.

00:11:12.389 --> 00:11:14.089
"What the hell, who pushed me?"

00:11:14.089 --> 00:11:17.240
He whirled around, but there was no one on
the stairs with him.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:21.870
Still, Mark could hear the sound of footsteps
hammering past Chase and toward him and Oliver.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.730
What happened next shocked him to his core.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:29.490
Oliver was dragged to his feet by the collar
of his shirt, pulled by an unseen force.

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:34.110
Then, with a loud thwack, something invisible
hit him square in the nose.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.110
"Ow!"

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.110
He cried out.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.880
But before he could react anymore, he was
dealt another blow to the stomach, doubling

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.260
over in pain.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:42.310
"What the-"

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.260
Something swept his legs out from under him,
and he fell hard, head hitting the floor with

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.260
a crack.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.740
Then, it was quiet.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:54.029
Oliver was still breathing but very much unconscious,
blood trickling from his nose.

00:11:54.029 --> 00:11:55.320
"Screw this!"

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.980
Chase yelled, bolting out the door.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:01.040
As Mark scrambled toward the door to follow
him, to run home before he could be attacked

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.840
next, he saw his backpack sliding across the
floor toward him.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:04.840
"Thanks for the sandwich."

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:08.490
A female voice said, though he couldn't see
the source.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.550
"I love peanut butter."

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:15.190
"You're welcome," he stammered, before grabbing
his bag and sprinting all the way home.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:19.480
As the story of the haunted house began to
spread, rumors and local news reports alike

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.250
reached the ears of the SCP Foundation.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:26.340
Foundation staff in the area placed infrared
cameras around the abandoned house, and the

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:29.459
footage captured a human heat signature.

00:12:29.459 --> 00:12:32.520
Whatever was in that house, it was no ghost.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.870
Using infrared cameras to track the entity,
it was quickly brought into custody.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:40.940
Before long, the entity was opening up to
the Foundation, and she offered to cooperate

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:44.020
willingly in exchange for warm food and shelter.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:50.440
So, the invisible woman was taken to a nearby
Foundation Site, and given the official classification:

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:51.660
SCP-347.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:57.690
SCP-347 is a young adult woman, standing at
approximately 164cm tall.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:04.589
For all intents and purposes, she is a completely
average woman, with one exception: she is

00:13:04.589 --> 00:13:07.139
completely invisible to the naked eye.

00:13:07.139 --> 00:13:11.839
This includes her body, as well as everything
inside of it including her blood, skin, and

00:13:11.839 --> 00:13:13.000
hair samples.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:18.320
Though the cones and rods of the human eye
must be visible in order to see, SCP-347's

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:22.040
vision has registered as normal following
extensive tests.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:26.649
She refers to herself with the name "Claudia,"
though this is assumed to be an alias inspired

00:13:26.649 --> 00:13:30.389
by Claude Rains, the lead actor in "The Invisible
Man."

00:13:30.389 --> 00:13:35.170
Her real identity, if she indeed has one,
has not yet been confirmed.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:40.980
Aside from her invisibility, SCP-347's only
other notable traits are an ability to pick

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:46.149
locks, a talent for thievery, and the ability
to swallow small objects in order to turn

00:13:46.149 --> 00:13:51.570
them invisible, and then cough them up at
a later time without any sickness or discomfort.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:57.200
She seems to crave human contact and socialization,
becoming frustrated when she is ignored.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:02.899
She will act out in these cases by pranking
people, and rearranging and hiding their things.

00:14:02.899 --> 00:14:06.940
When she is left alone with someone who is
sleeping, she has been known to stroke their

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:10.029
hair, touch their face, or tuck them in.

00:14:10.029 --> 00:14:13.470
She does this, she says, because it just feels
"right."

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:18.120
However, those it is done to tend to describe
the behavior as "unnerving."

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:24.050
Though she is invisible in terms of visible
light, she can be seen using infrared or ultraviolet

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.130
cameras.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:31.690
SCP-347 is currently contained at Site 1,
kept in a 5m x 5m room monitored with an infrared

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:32.690
camera.

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:37.860
The room has an attached bathroom complete
with a shower and bathtub, a queen-sized bed,

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:43.620
two armchairs, a desk and swivel chair, several
bookcases, a TV, and a DVD player.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:49.130
Her bookcases are filled with books, mainly
adventure stories, romance novels, and art

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:50.959
books, as per her request.

00:14:50.959 --> 00:14:55.480
She has also been permitted DVD copies of
any movies or television shows that she asks

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:59.959
for, as long as they pre-date her arrival
at the SCP Foundation.

00:14:59.959 --> 00:15:04.459
New releases may be added, but only after
prior approval from the research team.

00:15:04.459 --> 00:15:08.430
Though she does not frequently wear clothes,
she is to be provided with any clothing that

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:12.360
she requests, as well as a collection of makeup
and wigs.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:16.350
She has been encouraged to dress up to her
heart's content, as it allows Foundation staff

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.940
to more easily gauge her location at any given
time.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.330
While she is inside, the door to her room
must remain locked.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:27.730
At least two staff members must check her
door every hour for signs of tampering with

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:28.730
the lock.

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:33.430
The door may only be unlocked to allow staff
in and out for interviews, research, and the

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.360
delivery of meals and other requested items.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:41.339
She thoroughly enjoys human company, and will
chat, joke, and even flirt with those who

00:15:41.339 --> 00:15:42.690
visit her room.

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:47.650
She is permitted to leave her containment
if and only if she is accompanied by a staff

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:52.079
member with at least Level-2 security clearance,
as well as wearing a layer of grease paint

00:15:52.079 --> 00:15:54.449
on her face and gloves on her hands.

00:15:54.449 --> 00:15:57.810
This allows the staff to see her hands and
facial expressions.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:01.820
While she is out and about, staff are instructed
to treat her with respect and avoid making

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:07.269
any rude or crass comments about her invisibility,
or her state of dress - or undress.

00:16:07.269 --> 00:16:11.319
If she attempts to escape, she is to be returned
to her room and locked inside.

00:16:11.319 --> 00:16:16.490
If the staff are unable to detect SCP-347's
location, they will be given infrared heat

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:20.620
vision goggles and instructed to keep an eye
out for unusual phenomena.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:25.880
Dr. Rights added an addendum to her official
file, warning male personnel to politely decline

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:29.190
any advances that SCP-347 makes toward them.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.190
His note reads:

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.600
"She's an invisible kleptomaniac.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:35.741
When you leave, afterward, you're going to
realize three seconds too late that you don't

00:16:35.741 --> 00:16:39.490
have your keys in your pocket anymore, and
you will be held accountable for whatever

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:40.490
happens.

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:43.319
Besides, the last thing we need is an invisible
pregnancy.

00:16:43.319 --> 00:16:45.300
-Dr. Rights"

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:50.480
When she was first contained, SCP-347 had
regular violent outbursts and displayed signs

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:55.519
of emotional instability, including compulsive
theft and depressive episodes during which

00:16:55.519 --> 00:16:58.910
she would give all surrounding people the
silent treatment.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:03.430
Her condition has improved gradually over
time with the application of regular counseling

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:08.640
sessions intended to help her heal from the
trauma caused by years of complete isolation

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.569
and being unseen by the world around her.

00:17:11.569 --> 00:17:15.680
Several of the research staff studying Claudia
have suggested that she be introduced to other

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:21.250
SCPs, particularly those who are humanoid
and considered to be non-threatening.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:25.400
She might, they posit, benefit from social
interaction with other anomalous beings that

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:27.280
she can relate and connect to.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:32.680
This, in addition to her therapy, could improve
her mental and emotional state significantly.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:38.429
After all, just because she's invisible, that
doesn't mean she has to feel invisible too.

00:17:38.429 --> 00:17:42.429
Claudia has expressed a great deal of interest
in this idea, stating that it would be nice

00:17:42.429 --> 00:17:46.320
to have some friends on the inside who aren't
being paid to talk to her.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:50.679
Though no match-ups have been approved as
of yet, several anomalies have been proposed

00:17:50.679 --> 00:17:53.580
should the program be put into action.

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:58.460
SCP-507 was brought up in conversation by
more than one researcher, given his harmless

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:02.380
nature, friendly demeanor, and fascination
with the paranormal.

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:06.500
He supported the idea enthusiastically, stating
that he would be thrilled to meet a real live

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.340
invisible person.

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:13.210
SCP-343 has also asked to meet with Claudia,
believing he can potentially help her overcome

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:17.970
some of her emotional difficulties, and offer
her some much-needed comfort.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:24.289
Other potential anomalies to introduce to
Claudia include SCP-073 and SCP-056, though

00:18:24.289 --> 00:18:27.720
Claudia's flirtatious nature might complicate
the latter.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:32.650
Everybody wants to be known, to be acknowledged
and recognized for the person that they know

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:34.140
themselves to be.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:40.530
For SCP-347, it once seemed as if having that
simple desire, that human need, met, would

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.410
be impossible for her.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:47.919
But now, for better or for worse, as long
as she's in the custody of the SCP Foundation,

00:18:47.919 --> 00:18:50.980
Claudia can make something approximating a
normal life.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:53.710
She can, at last, be seen.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:59.861
Now go check out “SCP-811 - Swamp Woman”
and “SCP-953 - Polymorphic Humanoid” for

00:18:59.861 --> 00:19:03.730
even more lovely - and not so lovely - anomalous
ladies!

